@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-apply-json-patch-immutably-with-strict-pointer-validation
+type: decision-log
+title: "Apply JSON Patch immutably with strict pointer validation"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Services need to apply standard JSON Patch documents without exposing JavaScript property traversal
+or allowing callers to mutate the document passed to the shared toolkit.
+
+## Decision
+
+Clone the input document before applying operations, clone values when adding or copying them, and
+resolve every operation path using the same strict RFC 6901 rules as `resolvePointer`. Array insertion
+accepts only canonical indices and `-` only for `add`; object writes define own properties so special
+keys such as `__proto__` remain data rather than affecting prototypes.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Results have no mutable references into the input document, invalid or inherited path members fail,
+and `copy` creates an independent JSON value. Applying a patch requires cloning the JSON tree.
